{"title": "How to control unit tests in Agentic Pipelines", "link": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50437119", "summary": "<p>Have some wins but many struggles here<p>When generating new features using agents, we must then update the unit tests<p>This is counter to the purpose of unit tests.<p>Allowing the system to update its unit tests is introducing risk and uncertainty, even with scoped PRs<p>Not allowing the system to update unit tests will negatively impact velocity…<p>How are folks in the field handling this? Have a real rube-Goldberg situation going on here</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50437119\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50437119</a></p>\n<p>Points: 3</p>\n<p># Comments: 0</p>", "published": "2026-11-10T07:20:54+00:00", "source": "Hacker News Best", "category": "techblog", "matched_entities": {}, "ontology": {"repo": "BlogRadar", "category": "techblog", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "source_event_model": "blog_post", "event_model_id": "tech.blog_post", "evidence_policy_ids": ["source_metadata", "article_text"], "event_model_payload": {"headline": "How to control unit tests in Agentic Pipelines", "source_name": "Hacker News Best", "source_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50437119", "published_at": "2026-11-10T07:20:54+00:00", "summary": "<p>Have some wins but many struggles here<p>When generating new features using agents, we must then update the unit tests<p>This is counter to the purpose of unit tests.<p>Allowing the system to update its unit tests is introducing risk and uncertainty, even with scoped PRs<p>Not allowing the system to update unit tests will negatively impact velocity…<p>How are folks in the field handling this? Have a real rube-Goldberg situation going on here</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50437119\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50437119</a></p>\n<p>Points: 3</p>\n<p># Comments: 0</p>"}}, "logged_at": "2026-11-10T08:01:58.950939+00:00"}
